{"study_accession":"PRJNA988068","secondary_study_accession":"SRP446158","title":"Whole transcriptome analysis of EBV infected peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs)","description":"In order to gain insights into the intricate molecular alterations taking place following Epstein-Barr virus (EBV) infection in primary B-cells, we employed RNA-Seq to investigate the dynamic changes occurring within the cell transcriptome during the early stages of EBV infection (0, 2, and 4 days post infection). By analysing the transcriptomic data generated, our objective was to find novel pathways and mechanisms that may play pivotal roles in the EBV-induced transformation of B-cells, particularly during early stage of B-cell activation. Overall design: Peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs) were infected with wild type GFP-tagged EBV (B95.8 strain) and total RNA was isolated post 2 and 4 days of infection. Uninfected PBMCs were taken as experimental control.","pubmed":"38530845","geo_series":"","n_samples":5,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN36002580","study_accession":"PRJNA988068","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"4 days post EBV infection, Replicate 2","description":"4 days post EBV infection, Replicate 2","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM7512212","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2023-08-04","attributes":[["source_name","PBMCs"],["cell_type","PBMCs"],["time","4 day"],["treatment","Infected"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR25040728","experiment_accession":"SRX20795247","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"NextSeq 500","read_count":23171510,"base_count":3492807924,"first_public":"2023-08-04","experiment_title":"NextSeq 500 sequencing: GSM7512212: 4 days post EBV infection, Replicate 2 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN36002581","study_accession":"PRJNA988068","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","